{{Quote|You wanted to ''free'' your fellow Wookiees&mdash;well, now you can join them mining ore on Jabiim.|A First Order stormtrooper commander, to Chewbacca|<ref name="Ghosts of Kashyyyk, Part 3" />}}
'''Jabiim''' was a terrestrial [[planet]]<ref name="Part V audio">{{Kenobi|Part V}} &mdash; Audio description</ref> situated within the regions known as the [[Outer Rim Territories]]<ref name="TFABG" /> and [[the Slice]].<ref name="The Slice" /> Connected to [[Sy Myrth]] and [[Taskeed system|Taskeed]] by [[hyperspace route]]s, it was positioned at the coordinates S-7<ref name="TFABG" /> on the [[Standard Galactic Grid]].<ref name="Rebel Dossier">''[[Star Wars: Rogue One: Rebel Dossier]]''</ref> [[Ore]] was one of the main exports of Jabiim.<ref name="Ghosts of Kashyyyk, Part 3" />

==History==
By the [[Imperial Era]], Jabiim was a [[planet]] that had been largely forgotten by the galaxy.<ref name="JabiimDB">{{Databank|jabiim|Jabiim}}</ref> It was only known for its [[mining]] operations and as a way station for more desirable destinations,<ref name="DoR:TVG">''[[Star Wars: Dawn of Rebellion: The Visual Guide]]''</ref> becoming a dumping ground and sanitation depot.<ref name="Designing the Galaxy">{{HomeVideoCite|set=Obi-Wan Kenobi: The Complete Series|featurette=Designing the Galaxy}}</ref> Due to this reputation,<ref name="JabiimDB" /> the [[Hidden Path]], an underground network that helped [[Force-sensitive]]s escape [[Galactic Empire|Imperial]] persecution, used a [[Jabiim Hidden Path safehouse|safehouse]] on Jabiim as the penultimate destination on "the Path," in which [[Jedi]] and other Force-sensitives received new identities.<ref name="Part III">{{Kenobi|Part III}}</ref>

[[File:IntoTheBreach-OWKpV.png|thumb|left|270px|The [[Imperial Army]] attacks the Path compound on Jabiim.]]
In [[9 BBY]],<ref name="Timeline 9 BBY">{{KenobiDate|IV|the attack on Jabiim}}</ref> [[Obi-Wan Kenobi]], [[Tala Durith]], and young [[Princess]] [[Leia Skywalker Organa Solo|Leia Organa]] joined the rest of the Path in getting Leia to safety. However, Leia's companion droid, [[L0-LA59]] had been outfitted with a tracking device by the [[Reva Sevander|Third Sister]], allowing her and [[Anakin Skywalker|Darth Vader]] to follow them to the planet.<ref name="Part IV" /> During the [[Attack on Jabiim|attack]], the Path, Kenobi and Organa among them, managed to escape Vader's wrath. The Third Sister would also attempt to assassinate Vader soon after in revenge for his role in the Great Jedi Purge, but Vader humiliated the former Youngling and left her to die before revealing that the [[Grand Inquisitor]], whom she thought she had also assassinated, had survived.<ref name="Part V">{{Kenobi|Part V}}</ref>

During the [[First Order-Resistance War]], Jabiim fell under the control of the [[First Order]], who trafficked [[Wookiee]] [[Slavery|slaves]] from [[Kashyyyk]] to [[Mining|mine]] ore on Jabiim. When the [[Resistance]] operative [[Chewbacca]] was captured during the [[blockade of Kashyyyk]], a First Order [[Unidentified First Order stormtrooper commander (Kashyyyk)|stormtrooper commander]] planned to send him to Jabiim along with a group of slaves. With the assistance of a [[porg]] named [[Terbus]], however, Chewbacca managed to free the Wookiee [[prisoner]]s and escape enslavement.<ref name="Ghosts of Kashyyyk, Part 3" />

==Behind the scenes==
{{Quote|Poor Obi-Wan always has a tough time on Jabiim.|Matt Martin|<ref name="MattTweet">{{Twitter|missingwords|status/1537143650353696768|[[Matt Martin]]|date=2022-06-15|quote=Poor Obi-Wan always has a tough time on Jabiim.|archivefile=File:MattMartin-Jabiim-Twitter.png}}</ref>}}
[[File:Jabiim-FoC.jpg|thumb|right|300px|Jabiim, as it appears in the ''Star Wars'' Legends continuity]]
Jabiim was first shown in the new ''[[Star Wars]]'' [[canon]] on a [[map]] in the [[Star Wars: The Force Awakens Beginner Game|''Star Wars: The Force Awakens'' Beginner Game]], published by [[Fantasy Flight Games]] in [[2016]].<ref name="TFABG" /> It made its live-action debut in "[[Part IV]]" of the ''[[Star Wars: Obi-Wan Kenobi]]'' television series.<ref name="Part IV" /> As noted by artist [[Doug Chiang]], the team behind ''Obi-Wan Kenobi'' believed Jabiim had a very strong graphic design to it, which informed both its color palette and form as a crater. Taking inspiration from these designs, they designed Jabiim with the hope it would come across as a galactic dumping ground or sanitation depot.<ref name="Designing the Galaxy" />

In the [[Star Wars Legends|''Star Wars'' Legends]] continuity, [[Jabiim/Legends|Jabiim]] first appeared in the [[Star Wars comic books|comic]] [[Republic 55|''Republic'' 55]], written by [[W. Haden Blackman]], penciled by [[Brian Ching]], and published by [[Dark Horse Comics]]<ref name="Republic 55">[[Republic 55|''Republic'' 55]]</ref> on [[July 2]], [[2003]].<ref name="DH">{{DarkHorse|url=Comics/12-201/Star-Wars-Republic-55The-Battle-of-Jabiim-Part-1-of-4|text=Star Wars: Republic #55}}</ref> In Legends, it was depicted as a planet that had sided with the [[Confederacy of Independent Systems/Legends|Confederacy of Independent Systems]] during the [[Clone Wars/Legends|Clone Wars]] between the CIS and [[Galactic Republic/Legends|Galactic Republic]]. In response, the Republic launched an invasion<ref name="Republic 55" /> in [[22 BBY/Legends|22 BBY]]<ref name="LegendsDate">''[[The Essential Reader's Companion]]'' and {{FactFile2014|30|VEN 1-6|Asajj Ventress}} establish that the Battle of Jabiim of [[Star Wars Legends|''Star Wats'' Legends]] happened in the first few [[Standard month/Legends|months]] of the [[Clone Wars/Legends|Clone Wars]] and before the start of the ''[[Star Wars: The Clone Wars]]'' series in 22 BBY.</ref> and kicked off the grueling [[Battle of Jabiim]], which [[Obi-Wan Kenobi/Legends|Obi-Wan Kenobi]] took part in as a [[Jedi General/Legends|Jedi General]].<ref name="Republic 55" /> Following its appearance in the ''Obi-Wan Kenobi'' series, [[Matt Martin]] of the [[Lucasfilm Story Group]] compared its role in the Legends ''Republic'' comics and canon television series by joking about how Kenobi always seemed to have a tough time when he stepped foot on Jabiim.<ref name="MattTweet" />

